!Sample_submission_date = Oct 22 2021
!Sample_last_update_date = May 14 2022
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = Human melanoma
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell type: melanoma BLM cells
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = genotype: sgCtl
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = treatment: TNF 0h
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = treatment: untreated
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = 2×10E6 BLM sgCtl or sgRNF31 BLM human melanoma cells were pretreated with vehicle (DMSO) or HOIPIN-8 (10 µM) for 16 h, followed by TNF stimulation (100 ng/ml) for 0 or 6 hours.
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = Cells were cultured in DMEM supplemented with 9% fetal bovine serum (Sigma) plus 100 U/ml penicillin and 0.1 mg/ml streptomycin (Gibco).
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Cells were then lysed by adding 600 µl of buffer RLT (Qiagen, 79216) and their total RNA extracted using a RNeasy mini kit (Qiagen, 74106) according to the manufacturer’s instructions.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = PolyA+ stranded RNA Libraries were generated using the TruSeq Stranded mRNA sample preparation kit (Illumina)
!Sample_data_processing = Sequenced reads were trimmed for adaptor sequence, and masked for low-complexity or low-quality sequence
!Sample_data_processing = Mapped to the human reference genome hg38 using STAR (version 2.7) (Dobin et al., 2013) with default settings
!Sample_data_processing = Genes reads were counted using  HTSeq (Anders et al., 2015) (version 0.11.1)
!Sample_data_processing = Count data were analyzed in RStudio (version 1.4.1106) with DESeq2 (version1.30.1) (Love et al., 2014)
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: hg38
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: raw counts matrix
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: normalized counts matrix by DESeq2-rlog transformed
